## What is wrong (one paragraph)

The registrations for `POST /api/billing/checkout/custom` (`billing.openapi.ts:732`-`:757`) and `POST /api/billing/customers/{customerId}/default-payment-method` (`:871`-`:897`) declare their request body as a multi-line `body: {` block whose only key is `content:` (`:740`, `:880`), with no `required`, so the published spec says the body is OPTIONAL. The handlers say otherwise: `routes/billing.ts:409` (`router.post('/checkout/custom', ...)`) runs `PurchaseCustomSchema.parse(req.body)` (`:411`; the schema at `:120`-`:125` requires quantity, successUrl, cancelUrl) and maps a `ZodError` to 400 (`:440`-`:442`); `:546` (`router.post('/customers/:customerId/default-payment-method', ...)`) destructures `paymentMethodId` from `req.body` (`:548`) and answers 400 when it is missing or not a string (`:551`-`:554`). The service runs express 4 (`package.json:18`), whose json parser leaves `req.body` as an empty object when no body is sent, so both handlers answer 400 for an absent body. KS-1364's sweep 4 measured exactly that: checkout/custom 1 case (`"path":["quantity"],"message":"Required"`, not baselined), default-payment-method 2 cases, both 400. The ticket's direction is verbatim: "mark `requestBody.required: true` where the handler's Zod schema rejects an absent body, at the generator (`*.openapi.ts`)". In the multi-line form the house shape is a `required: true,` line inside the `body:` block (`kyc.openapi.ts:474`).

