## UNMEASURED - stated rather than glossed

- No Schemathesis run. That the `positive_data_acceptance` no-body cases stop firing for `POST /api/billing/checkout/custom` and `POST /api/billing/customers/{customerId}/default-payment-method` is a prediction from the rendered spec (a `required: true` request body means a conforming generator no longer sends an empty one), not a measurement. A live re-check needs a running stack; KS-1380's build problem was reported for other services and was not re-measured here.
- The SERVED contract (`/api/docs/openapi.json` through the gateway) was not read; the gateway serves `docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml`, so it needs the regenerated YAML to land (see Scope).
- That the handler answers 400 for an ABSENT body was read at source (a zod `object` rejects `undefined`/`{}`) and is what KS-1364's sweep 4 measured live (`status 400`); it was not re-run in-process here.
- node_modules: the workspace root is symlink-farmed from the `sparkfeed` checkout (installed at `94c9c7aa`); billing has its own `package-lock.json`, but farming its modules in makes `tsc` FAIL rc 2 (two `@types/pg` copies, TS2345 in `src/db.ts:45`), so billing runs on the root farm alone, where tsc is rc 0 at tip and golden. Between `94c9c7aa` and the tip the root lock moved (KS-1378's axios/dompurify refresh among others); zod, zod-to-openapi and vitest were not re-verified as identical to a fresh `npm ci` at the tip.
- The YAML companion was generated in this writer's scratch clone (`npm run generate-openapi`); it stacks with the other five KS-1364 carves' companions (measured: all six product goldens and all six companions apply strictly in sequence on one tree), and the KS-1015 envelope READY's companion still applies on top (`git apply --check`, measured). That the STACKED YAML equals a fresh `generate-openapi` of the stacked tree was NOT run.

